id: pm-1eted6
title: "GH-926: warn before a stale pm binary mutates a project pinned to a newer CLI/SDK"
description: "A PATH-resolved pm binary older than the project dependency or lockfile can perform tracker mutations without warning, risking schema, history, merge-fence, validation, and SDK drift."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T08:33:01.251Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T08:47:20.241Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Before any mutating command, pm detects when the executing binary is older than the project-declared or lockfile-resolved CLI/SDK version and emits a deterministic actionable refusal or explicit acknowledgement path; read-only commands remain available for diagnosis; unit, integration, packaged npx/bunx, and stale-binary negative-control tests prove the guard without reading the real tracker"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: "Read paths expose a structured version mismatch and mutation paths fail closed unless an explicit recovery override is supplied, with package-manager-neutral remediation."
actual_result: Older global and stale local binaries mutate a project whose declared and locked pm-cli version is newer without any diagnostic.
affected_version: 2026.8.6
component: CLI bootstrap and workspace compatibility
